Description: A traceable functional-interpretation and hypothesis-generation
    layer after transcriptomic analysis. Target-specific GOseq enrichment
    remains the experimental anchor while the same experiment-matched portable
    foreground and tested background are evaluated across researcher-selected
    g:Profiler organism annotation contexts. Scoreless, provenance-linked
    evidence profiles describe target support, annotation-context recurrence,
    alternative-context hypotheses, identifier representability, and
    context-effective recognition. Optional RRvGO semantic summarization keeps
    target-supported and hypothesis terms separate. Source-specific statistics
    are never combined across contexts. The framework supports both
    reference-rich and annotation-limited studies, including de novo
    transcriptomes, without claiming orthology, conservation, or integrated
    significance.
